{
 "id": "2026-11-11-c",
 "title": "Why is nothing ever really free? 🎟️",
 "description": "Every choice has a hidden price tag: opportunity cost, the value of the best option you gave up. Even economists trip on it: in a 2005 survey of almost 200 economists, only 21.6% got a simple opportunity-cost question right, fewer than random guessing would.\n\nSources: https://www.econlib.org/library/Enc/OpportunityCost.html ; https://www.viet-studies.com/kinhte/Econ_OpCost_NYT.pdf",
